  "qFood1": "What should I eat every day?",
  "aFood1": "Eat something from each group every day: rice or ragi, dal or egg, and green vegetables. Add a little jaggery and groundnut. Drink water often. Take your iron tablet after food.",
  "qFood2": "Can I drink tea and coffee?",
  "aFood2": "A little is fine, but not right after your iron tablet — it stops the iron from working. Leave one hour between them. Milk, buttermilk and water are better through the day.",
  "qFood3": "I feel sick in the morning. What can I do?",
  "aFood3": "Eat small amounts more often instead of three big meals. Dry food like puffed rice or a biscuit before getting out of bed helps. If you cannot keep any food or water down for a day, tell your ASHA worker.",

  "qRest1": "How much should I rest?",
  "aRest1": "Rest for two hours in the day, lying on your left side. Sleep well at night. In the last three months your body needs more rest than usual.",
  "qRest2": "Can I do my usual housework?",
  "aRest2": "Light work is good for you. Avoid lifting heavy pots or water, standing for many hours, and climbing. If you feel giddy or your stomach tightens, stop and sit down.",
  "qRest3": "Can I travel to my mother's village?",
  "aRest3": "Short journeys are usually fine until the eighth month. Avoid long bumpy road journeys near your delivery date, and always carry your Thayi Card with you.",

  "qAfter1": "When should I start feeding the baby?",
  "aAfter1": "Feed the baby within the first hour after birth. The first thick yellow milk is very important — do not throw it away. Give only breast milk for six months, no water and no honey.",
  "qAfter2": "How long should I rest after delivery?",
  "aAfter2": "Take full rest for six weeks. Eat well and keep drinking water. Your ASHA worker will visit you at home several times during this period.",
  "qAfter3": "When is the baby's first vaccine?",
  "aAfter3": "The first vaccines are given at birth itself in the hospital. The next set is at six weeks. Keep the immunisation card safe and take it to every visit.",

  "aFallback": "I am not able to answer that one properly. Your ASHA worker will know — shall I pass this question to her?",
  "aMedicineRefusal": "I cannot advise you about medicines or doses. Please ask your ASHA worker or the doctor at your health centre — they know your record.",
